  "notes": "USAGE: Used as a noun or with ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ to form the verb {威嚇|いかく}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (to intimidate, to threaten).\n\nNUANCE: {威嚇|いかく} refers to threatening behavior intended to frighten or deter. It's used in various contexts: military (warning shots), animal behavior (territorial displays), and interpersonal intimidation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {威嚇|いかく}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (to intimidate, threaten)\n- {威嚇|いかく}⟦{射撃|しゃげき}→射撃：16089_shageki⟧ (warning shot)\n- {威嚇|いかく}⟦{行為|こうい}→行為：10021_koui⟧ (intimidating behavior)\n- {威嚇|いかく}⟦{的|てき}→〜的：09839_teki⟧な (threatening, intimidating)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{威圧|いあつ}→威圧：09165_iatsu⟧ (coercion, pressure)\n- ⟦{脅|おど}す→脅す：27206_odosu⟧ (to threaten)\n- ⟦{脅迫|きょうはく}→脅迫：27205_kyouhaku⟧ (threat, intimidation - more serious)\n- {恫喝|どうかつ} (intimidation, browbeating - stronger)",
